{
	title: '/clear: fresh context in the same tab',
	spec: "/clear (src/host/commands/clear.ts) writes a history record {type: reset} on an idle session: provider input rebuilds from the records after the latest reset alone, with no summary, so the model starts fresh with the same system prompt, cwd and model. The screen clears too: every client shows only what follows the latest reset, live, after a reload and after a host restart, starting with an output message 'Context cleared.' with its timestamp (not a divider rule). Scrolling up loads nothing from before it; the history file keeps every record, as nothing is deleted. The status row's context figure drops with the context until the next round reports one. Drafts, the session name and the tab stay. A running turn answers that it is busy. A compact summary is context too: /clear right after /compact still writes the reset, and only a context empty since a reset (or never used) is already fresh. Tests: provider input after /clear holds only later records, and the live view equals a reloaded one, starting at the message; a compact after a reset summarises only records after the reset; /clear after /compact drops the summary.",
	status: 'done',
