		"Built on bc: the {type: reset} record, its replay slice and divider text live with compact (common/replay.ts, transcript.boundary, host/compact.ts compact.reset). /clear on a context already empty since the last boundary says 'the context is already empty' and writes nothing.",
		"Screen: transcript.fromSnapshot starts at the latest reset and drops stand-ins; the live divider event carries clear and ts, and fold replaces all items with the message (the session is idle). Snapshots and history pages that hold a reset offer no older page (pages.snapshotSteps, host.ts history), so the terminal's fetch-all and web scroll-back stop there. stats.lastContext stops at a compact or reset, and compact.boundary drops stats.state.context and sends turn-stats: without that the old figure survived /clear and every reload. History files never rotate (the old Hal's currentLog did); hiding was chosen over rotation to avoid repointing marks, pages and the context page."
